WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.470
31 January 1953.

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:09.030
A North Sea flood drowns 1,836
people in the Netherlands.

3
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:15.850
Today, Singapore's mean sea level may
rise by up to 1.15 metres by 2100.

4
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.710
About 30 per cent of the island is less
than 5 metres above mean sea level.

5
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:25.190
Its prime minister guessed protection
would cost 100 billion Singapore dollars

6
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:27.050
over 100 years.

7
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.950
How can a city prepare
for risks it cannot stop?

8
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.130
In this mission, you'll go to Rotterdam,
where the Maeslant Barrier's 2 gates

9
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.130
are each 210 metres wide.

10
00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:42.750
Then you'll weigh climatic and geopolitical
risks for an island importing over

11
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:45.030
90 per cent of its food.

12
00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.870
Your mission: explain how a city can
prepare for risks it cannot stop.
